.TH SITU-EDIT-GUI 1 "" "situ" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
situ-edit-gui \- read and edit a message against a situ schema, in a window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B situ-edit-gui
.RI [ options ]
.I schema
.I message
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B situ-edit-gui
is
.BR situ\-edit (1)
as a Qt window: the message's fields as a table, edited in their cells, a
nested struct opened in its own window, and the verdict beside them. The
message opened is never overwritten; Save writes where
.B \-\-out
names. With
.B \-\-tui
the same window is drawn on the terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-struct " NAME"
Which layout to read the message as.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " N"
Where the struct starts in the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-length " N"
How long its frame is.
.TP
.BI \-\-arg " N"
A value for a
.B parameter
member, in order.
.TP
.B \-\-hex
The message file holds hex rather than bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " NAME=VALUE"
Store a value, as
.BR situ\-edit (1)
does.
.TP
.BI \-\-set\-bytes " NAME=HEX"
Store a byte run.
.TP
.BI \-\-insert " NAME:N=HEX"
Put an element into a run of structs.
.TP
.BI \-\-remove " NAME:N"
Take an element out of a run of structs.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Where Save writes.
.TP
.BI \-\-open " FIELD"
Open the nested struct in this field in its own window;
.I FIELD:N
for element
.I N
of a run of structs. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ui
Apply the edits through the window, print the table, write
.BR \-\-out ,
and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-keys " FIELD=SPEC"
Open the field's editor and press keys into it.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
The same window on this terminal, drawn by qtty.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
A window, even with no display in the environment.
.TP
.BI \-\-snapshot " COLSxROWS"
With
.BR \-\-tui :
print the window as the terminal shows it, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-scheme
Print whether the desktop reads as dark, light or unknown, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-window\-icon
Print whether the window has an icon to draw, and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR situ\-edit (1),
.BR situ\-edit\-tui (1),
.BR situc (1)
